hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1064","Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail bin Aliya narrated to us, Ayyoub narrated to us, and Ma’mal bin Hisham narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, On the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Amr ibn Wahb, he said: We were with Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, and he was asked: “Is she the mother of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?” Did anyone from this nation other than Abu Bakr say: Yes, we were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, so he mentioned the length of the hadith, and they said: Then We rode and the people overtook us. Abd al-Rahman bin Awf came forward and led them in one rak’ah, and he was in the second rak’ah. I went to call him to prayer and he forbade me. So we prayed the rak’ah that we had overtaken the one that preceded us, and Ma’mal said: And we performed the one that preceded us.”"
"1065","On the authority of Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If Prayer is rewarded, so do not go to it while you are running, but go to it and rest in peace. Whatever you catch up with, pray, and whatever you miss, complete it, for he is one of you If he intends to pray, then he is in prayer.”"
